  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The envelope – passing chain and finish",
  "description": "Four cones make an envelope in front of one goal, with a player at each cone. Everyone else lines up with all the balls. The first in line plays a firm pass to the player at the first cone, who passes straight on to the next, and so on until the ball reaches the player at the cone above the goal, who shoots.\n\nRight after each pass, run after the ball and take the spot at the next cone. The shooter joins the back of the line. The drill uses half the court. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the floor to the receiver's blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Run to the next cone straight after your pass."
    }
  ],
